  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Louisiana's 4th Congressional District, encompassing northwestern Louisiana including Shreveport and Bossier City, holds its general election on November 3, 2026. Incumbent Republican U.S. House Speaker Mike Johnson seeks re-election against two Republican primary challengers (Joshua Morott and Mike Nichols) and two Democratic challengers (Conrad Cable and Matt Gromlich). Party primaries were originally scheduled for May 16, 2026, but were postponed by Governor Jeff Landry after the Supreme Court's ruling in Louisiana v. Callais, which required congressional map redrawing. The district is heavily Republican (Cook PVI: R+26), and Johnson's status as Speaker of the House makes this one of the most high-profile House races in Louisiana.",
